# spec: plr-d10-redesign-real-integration-2026-10-25 (H1) - the founder's TEST COPY of the app
# ("ShramSafal TEST", app id com.agrisync.shramsafal.test). Copy to `.env.fieldtest` (gitignored), set the
# TEST server's address, then: `npm run build:fieldtest` -> `npx cap sync android` -> Gradle `assembleFieldtest`.
#
# NEVER put the live server (https://api.shramsafal.in) here: the test copy runs new code that must not write
# into real farms. All VITE_* values are public (inlined into the bundle) - no secrets.
#
# Example for a test server on the founder's PC on his home Wi-Fi (PENDING D-21):
VITE_AGRISYNC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.10:5048

# The test copy must show what the live release shows: the same DFES companion flags as
# .github/workflows/release.yml (Build web assets). Without them the approved Shram Sathi waiting
# screen, the understanding meter and the question panel stay off in the test copy.
VITE_UNDERSTANDING_METER=1
VITE_STAGE_QUESTIONS=1
VITE_DISCIPLINE_SYSTEM=1
VITE_VOICE_CONTINUITY=1
VITE_DAILY_LOOP=1
VITE_TASK_CLOSE_CONFIRM=1
VITE_UNLOCK_COUNTER_PAUSED=1
VITE_SIMULATE_UNLOCK=0
